@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Acceptable Use Policy (AUP) — SaveZonix";
}

<section class="legal-page">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
        <partial name="_LegalNav" model='(string)"AcceptableUse"' />

        <div class="legal-header">
            <h1 class="legal-title">Acceptable Use Policy</h1>
            <div class="legal-meta">
                <span>Safe Computing Standards &bull; Prohibited Activities</span>
                <span>Last Updated: September 15, 2026</span>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="legal-content">
            <div class="highlight-box">
                <strong>Purpose:</strong> This Acceptable Use Policy defines the standards and limitations governing the lawful, ethical, and safe operation of the SaveZonix software utility and web engine.
            </div>

            <h2>1. Core Principles</h2>
            <p>SaveZonix is developed to foster fair personal access, network protocol research, and authorized media archiving. Users are expected to utilize the software responsibly without degrading network infrastructure or infringing upon the legal rights of content owners.</p>

            <h2>2. Permitted Uses</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Downloading open-access educational lectures, public domain video archives, and Creative Commons media.</li>
                <li>Archiving personal live streams or self-created video broadcasts for offline preservation.</li>
                <li>Analyzing network media transport mechanisms, HLS playlists, and chunked delivery pipelines for research and development.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>3. Strictly Prohibited Uses</h2>
            <p>You agree not to use SaveZonix for any of the following unauthorized activities:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Commercial Piracy:</strong> Downloading, selling, redistributing, or publicly broadcasting copyrighted commercial cinema, subscription television, or pay-per-view events without authorization.</li>
                <li><strong>DRM Circumvention:</strong> Attempting to tamper with, decrypt, or reverse-engineer hardware-level DRM protection systems (Widevine L1/L3, Apple FairPlay, Microsoft PlayReady).</li>
                <li><strong>Abusive Infrastructure Scraping:</strong> Launching automated, distributed denial-of-service (DDoS) loops or high-frequency batch requests that disrupt third-party hosting networks.</li>
                <li><strong>Harmful Content:</strong> Capturing, storing, or transmitting illegal material or content that violates statutory criminal laws.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>4. Enforcement &amp; Reporting</h2>
            <p>Failure to adhere to this policy constitutes a material breach of our Terms of Service. If you become aware of any abusive activity involving our software, please report it immediately to <a href="mailto:savezonix@gmail.com" class="auth-link">savezonix@gmail.com</a>.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
